-- title:
--   Strict ordinarity at p of the Taylor–Wiles Hecke-ring representation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, and let $p$ be a prime with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over the residue field $k$ of $\mathcal O$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space with an action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ trivial on some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$), absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no proper non-zero invariant subspace. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N\neq 0$, let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a non-unit and every $\sigma$ acting as $x\mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, let $\pi_i\colon(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ be homomorphisms and $\alpha_i\in k$; put $L=N\,(\prod_i q_i)\,r$ and $H_Q=H_r\cap\ker\pi_Q\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$. Assume the commutation hypotheses `OpComm` and `DiaComm` for the corresponding operators, and let $T$ be the resulting Hecke ring, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}$ of the Hecke module generated by its Hecke generators. Assume $T$ is local, Noetherian, complete for its maximal-adic topology, a finite $\mathcal O$-module, that $\mathcal O\to T$ is a local homomorphism and that $\mathcal O\to T\to T/\mathfrak m_T$ is surjective. Let $\rho'$ be an adic Galois representation over $T$ (a free $T$-module of rank two with adically continuous Galois action) whose trace at each Frobenius $\sigma$ at a prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ equals the Hecke operator $T_\ell$ in $T$, and whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Assume finally $p\mid L$, $p^2\nmid L$, and that $\bar\rho$, viewed as an adic representation over the field $k$, is not flat at $p$: it fails the condition that $k$ be finite and that every quotient of its underlying space by $I$ times itself, for $I$ an ideal with finite quotient, be Galois-equivariantly the set of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring of $\mathbb Q$ of rationals with denominator prime to $p$. Then $\rho'$ is strictly ordinary at $p$: $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $T$ and, for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit, there is a $T$-submodule $L_0$ of the underlying module spanned by the first vector of some basis, stable under the decomposition group of $P$, with $\rho'(\sigma)v-v\in L_0$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup and all $v$, and such that each $\sigma$ in the decomposition group admits $x,z\in T$ with $\rho'(\sigma)$ acting on $L_0$ by $x$, acting by $z$ modulo $L_0$, and $x-a z\in(p^n)$ whenever $\sigma$ raises every $p^n$-th root of unity to the power $a$.
--
--   This is the local condition at $p$ (Wiles's "strict" case) satisfied by the Galois representation carried by the Taylor–Wiles-level Hecke ring on the branch where the level is exactly divisible by $p$ and the residual representation is not finite flat at $p$. It feeds the construction of the modular deformation over the Hecke ring acting on the cohomological Hecke module, via [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary).
